      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a very edge case, but when you have 999+ prefabs where majority is from a large UI pack and you only have all of it there while testing and trying to figure out what to use.\nIn my case, I added a UI pack that was originally made in Unity 2019, so all prefabs had missing scripts because the UI components are different (for some reason). So I'm sitting there waiting for all those \"The referenced script (Unknown) on this Behaviour is missing!\" to load in the console, which takes a while when you have 999+ prefabs where all have missing links.\nThis is fixed/mitigated by simply excluding the folder in the UdonEditorManager when it's getting all prefab asset paths.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
